The family crest is the left Mitsudomoe.
The Saionji family was founded by FUJIWARA no Michisue, the third son of FUJIWARA no Kinzane.
When Michisue's great-grandson, Kintsune SAIONJI, was confined to the Imperial Court as a relative of the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) at the time of the Jokyu War, he was imprisoned as a relative of the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun), and after the war, he was trusted by the bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) and gained the real power of the Imperial Court as Kanto moshitsugi (an official in charge of the affairs of state) and raised the family status as Daijo-daijin (Grand minister of state
The family name of Saien-ji Temple is derived from the name of a temple built in a villa built by Kintsune in Kyoto (Kitayama-sho, Kadono-gun, Yamashiro Province).
This hall was also called Kitayama-dono, and the current Kinkaku-ji Temple was built by Yoshimitsu ASHIKAGA from the Saionji family.
Since Kintsune, he received support from the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) and had power over the Sekke (line of regents and advisers) throughout the Kamakura period.
