However, after his son, Kinhira SAIONJI, the Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama) had a distance from the bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun), he supported the Jimyoin-to (imperial lineage from Emperor Gofukakusa to Emperor Gokomatsu) and deepened conflict with the Daikakuji-to (imperial lineage starting with Emperor Kameyama).
After that, the Kamakura bakufu (Japanese feudal government headed by a shogun) was destroyed by Kinmune SAIONJI and was dismissed from the post of Kanto moshitsugi.
Kinmune sheltered Yasuie HOJO (Tokiokioki) who was the remnants of the Hojo clan, and tried to assassinate Emperor Godaigo, who started the Kenmu Restoration, and planned a rebellion that supported the Retired Emperor GofDaigo of Jimyoin-to (imperial lineage from Emperor Gofukakusa to Emperor Gokomatsu), and Kinshige SAIONJI, his younger brother, was arrested and executed.
