Mt. Hiei is a mountain located in the western part of Otsu City, Shiga Prefecture and the northern part of Kyoto Prefecture.
It is a generic name for the twin Mimi Mine, which is located on the border between Otsu City and Sakyo Ward, Kyoto City (8.38 meters) and Shimeigatake located in Sakyo Ward, Kyoto City.
The triangle triangle of Mt. Hiei is located in Otsu City.
It is considered to be a mountain of worship as well as Mt. Koya, and it flourished as Enryaku-ji Temple and Hiyoshi-taisha Shrine.
It is included in Higashiyama (Kyoto Prefecture).
It is also known as Mt. Hiei, Hokurei, Mt. Tendai, and Fuji.
Summary
It is located in the northeast east of Kyoto, and Mt. Hiei was regarded as a mountain for the defense of O-jo Castle.
