After Enryaku-ji Temple was opened on Mt. Hie, Oyamakui no kami was regarded as the guardian deity of the Tendai sect and Enryaku-ji Temple, and Sanno-shinko belief spread widely to Oyamakui-no-kami.
It is also a mountain of Enryaku-ji Temple on the top of Mt. Hiei and Mt. Nikko-taisha Shrine at the foot of Mt. Hiei.
To climb the mountain, there are Unbozaka, which is climbing from Shugakuin, Sakyo Ward, Kyoto City, and Mudo-ji Temple from Monzen-cho, Shiga Prefecture (Otsu City) to Mudo-ji valley via Mudo-ji Temple.
Unbozaka has been a road where monks, armed priests, and Imperial envoy sent to Enryaku-ji Temple in Kyoto since ancient times, and many climbers are still climbing.
