After that, after the first conquest of Choshu, he worked hard for the Imperial sanction of the Treaty of Amity and Commerce between the United States and Japan, and succeeded in obtaining the Imperial sanction for the Imperial sanction.
In the second conquest of Choshu in 1866, Yoshinobu ordered the Choshu Conquest to suppress the intervention of Satsuma Domain.
However, the bakufu army refused to dispatch troops to Satsuma Domain, which had formed the Satsuma-Choshu Alliance, and the bakufu army was defeated.
On July 20, when the Second conquest of Choshu, Shogun Iemochi died at Osaka-jo Castle.
