He was recommended to be the successor of Iemochi, but Yoshinobu refused it.
On August 20, the Tokugawa Shogun family inherited the position of Shogun, but refused to assume the position of Shogun.
After that, roju (member of shogun's council of elders) asked him to assume the position of Shogun, but he did not accept it, and on January 5, he was appointed as Shogun by the Emperor Komei.
In other words, this was a purpose to make a new shogun, and to make a political interest in politics.
Yoshinobu received the support of 240 million dollars from France through the French legation of leon LEO, and established Yokosuka iron factory and Shusen-jo Castle, and invited military advisors such as Julbern, and reformed the military system.
He also encouraged his younger brother Akitake TOKUGAWA to study in the Paris World Exposition, such as sending his real younger brother Akitake TOKUGAWA to the Paris World Exposition.
