As a local train connecting Kyoto and Nara, many foreign tourists use not only Japanese but also foreign tourists.
All trains are operated with four-car or six-car trains on the JR West Japan Railway Company (JR West).
In the double-track section, the maximum speed is 1,110 km/h, and other trains are 95 km/h.
The standard time is about 44 minutes from Kyoto, and about 47 minutes from Nara Station to Nara Station is approximately 47 minutes.
The trains bound for Kyoto stop at Kamikoma Station or Tanakura Station on the way to Nara Station, and there are some differences between the inbound and outbound trains and outbound trains.
